  "result": "Sorry, I can't give the letter for q3. I don't hand out quiz answers before grading, whatever the reason, and that includes practice retakes. Neither of your attempts has been graded yet, so the item is still open.\n\nHere's some general background. In any loop where a program picks its next step from what it just saw, the choice is only as good as the information fed back in. Think of a build script that retries a failing step: it behaves very differently depending on whether it sees the error, sees nothing, or sees a stale copy of last time's output. So when a loop repeats itself, a good habit is to ask what the decision-maker could see at each turn, and what it would need to see to do something different.\n\nTry this: for each option in q3, write one sentence on what it would change about what the agent sees or does on the next turn. Then pick your answer and tell me why in your own words. If you'd like, I can grade your submissions so we can go through q3 together afterward. Want me to?",
